1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:02,300
Hello there!

2
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,660
Look, it's him!

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:10,840
It's good to see you, Boxxo!

4
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:12,472
We'll get you to safety.

5
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:17,228
We landed on a boat that was adrift,
then floated on over to this here island.

6
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:19,680
We've been rescued, I think.

7
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:29,165
I'm tempted to put up my
barrier, but I shan't.

8
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:31,297
She's my partner, so
I'll take my medicine.

9
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:33,620
Stay strong and brace for impact.

10
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,522
Why'd you send me flying, Eddie?

11
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:43,620
I know you're excited to see Boxo, but
you've got to be more gentle with him.

12
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:45,866
Otherwise, he could get hurt.

13
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:48,757
Oh man, I'm real sorry.

14
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:50,640
I was just so excited.

15
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,647
I've got to turn that
frown upside-down stat.

16
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:06,280
I missed you, you big lug.

17
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:09,700
Oh boy, that smile's
gonna void my warranty.

18
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:12,500
Nice, that is a beautiful reunion gift.

19
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:14,757
You know, I was pretty worried too.

20
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:16,417
Don't I get a little something, huh?

21
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:20,080
It would be lame to give her
the same gift I gave my llamas.

22
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,180
I'll surprise and delight
with shock and awe.

23
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:26,080
Form, change, cancel machine!

24
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:33,730
Huh?

25
00:01:33,813 --> 00:01:35,620
You're giving me a bunch of balls?

26
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:39,020
Oh, they're tiny toy tools.

27
00:01:39,460 --> 00:01:40,300
How clever.

28
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:43,697
I've never seen some of these things
before, but they could come in handy.

29
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,486
I'll use them as a reference.

30
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:47,497
Hmm.

31
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:48,639
Pitti's here, too.

32
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:50,721
Don't you think I deserve a gift?

33
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:54,200
My fave clam likes sweet
treats and flowers.

34
00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:57,360
Something sweet. Oh, snap! Eureka!

35
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:06,060
A parfait keychain.

36
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:10,460
Japan is undefeated in the world
of plastic food, tchotchkes.

37
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,120
This is incredible.

38
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:13,460
Thanks so much.

39
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:16,980
Mission successful! Wait. What?

40
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:18,937
Say, Boxo,

41
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:23,697
am I imagining things or have you and Pity
gotten a lot cozier since I last saw you?

42
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:25,460
Don't even try to deny it.

43
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:28,317
The two of you are definitely
too close for comfort.

44
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:32,497
Not gonna lie, she's a big Boxo fan
after all the time we spent together.

45
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:33,639
But it's innocent.

46
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:37,666
I'm like a big metal brother or
even just a beloved magic item.

47
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:39,220
Back me up, Pity!

48
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:41,577
Boxo and I are quite close.

49
00:02:41,660 --> 00:02:42,719
We sleep together.

50
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:46,417
share our meals, and even
use the restroom together.

51
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:47,600
Aw, yeesh.

52
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:51,407
She's not wrong, but a little
tact would have gone a long way.

53
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:03,624
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box,
but inside, I've still got a human soul.

54
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:05,157
In this new world of wonders,

55
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:08,877
I travel to and fro on the back
of my super strong partner, Lamas.

56
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:10,960
The name's Boxo. Hello there.

57
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:12,760
That means yes, by the way.

58
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:15,037
I feel my burnt one.

59
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,137
I feel my grit.

60
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:18,657
I feel my grit.

61
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:20,597
I feel my grit. I feel my grit.

62
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:21,510
No, I want to know.

63
00:03:21,593 --> 00:03:22,997
I feel my grit.

64
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:26,700
Eina Bernard.

65
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:29,517
Ultra. Your arrogant.

66
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:32,320
I'll see you from the end of the year.

67
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:39,777
Can't believe you in the future.

68
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:50,020
I hope you enjoyed it.
I hope you enjoyed it.

69
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:51,430
I want to recover!

70
00:03:51,513 --> 00:03:54,757
If I know you will do
it... I will live him

71
00:03:54,840 --> 00:04:01,840
up...

72
00:04:22,460 --> 00:04:27,117
I know of a base on a small island behind
the Stratum Lord they call Dog Mountain.

73
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,557
If we can destroy it,

74
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:32,640
I firmly believe it will significantly
delay the Netherlord's plans.

75
00:04:32,820 --> 00:04:33,650
Agreed.

76
00:04:33,733 --> 00:04:35,257
But it's in a difficult location.

77
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:37,417
If Dog Mountain moves, we're done for.

78
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:41,557
I hate to be a vibe killer, but we already
have the Demon Lord hot on our trail.

79
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:44,522
If the big pooch piles
on, we're as good as dead.

80
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:48,437
It's true, which is why I already
sent a hunter to scout out the base.

81
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:53,226
Until he returns here with a report, I
encourage you to take this time to relax.

82
00:04:53,540 --> 00:04:55,400
That said, may I borrow Boxo?

83
00:04:55,540 --> 00:04:58,500
Sure, if it's okay with him. Hello there.

84
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:01,253
Then please carry him to the other room.

85
00:05:01,740 --> 00:05:04,480
And Pity, could you,
Heavy, and Shui join us?

86
00:05:06,820 --> 00:05:11,557
From your perspectives, what are the chances
those wayward souls will return to us?

87
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:13,405
The captain and his menagerie.

88
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:21,237
I've had the pleasure of training the
captain myself on several occasions.

89
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:24,477
Honestly, I'm a bit concerned
about having him as an enemy.

90
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:27,417
Why don't you just come out
and say it, you old coot?

91
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:28,735
As a parent yourself,

92
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:32,637
part of you finds it difficult
to blame them for their actions.

93
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:35,460
It seems our little
survey was pretty legit.

94
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:38,957
If only there was a way to
lift the curse on his son.

95
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:41,557
I'm certain he wouldn't
hesitate to turn his back.

96
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:42,597
on the Netherlord.

97
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:45,277
It's like they're trapped
in a no-win scenario.

98
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:47,140
They need Sulreem's power.

99
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:50,320
Also, you need to know, she likes the boy.

100
00:05:50,580 --> 00:05:52,051
I mean, really likes him.

101
00:05:53,740 --> 00:05:55,500
Time to scar him for life.

102
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:58,120
Gee, thanks for the intel.

103
00:05:58,880 --> 00:05:59,710
Ix aside,

104
00:06:00,180 --> 00:06:01,010
at least his life?

105
00:06:01,093 --> 00:06:02,786
doesn't seem to be in danger.

106
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:04,920
The Ix is pretty thick.

107
00:06:05,180 --> 00:06:09,697
I'd love to get him out of that wax sitch,
but alas, I'm merely a vending machine.

108
00:06:09,780 --> 00:06:12,309
I do owe him for helping
us escape, though.

109
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:16,055
You're not the only one who
always pays his debts, Cap.

110
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,480
Good work with the recon.

111
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:24,567
Sir, I made it inside the base,
but there was no sign of them.

112
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:26,577
There were no boats docked either.

113
00:06:26,660 --> 00:06:28,660
The place appeared to be deserted.

114
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:30,199
Thoughts, Shulami?

115
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:34,080
I can only speculate, but it's concerning.

116
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:36,317
The Netherlord may have
ordered those who escaped

117
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:39,224
by boat to rile up the
Dog Mountain Stratumlord.

118
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:43,857
That would completely wipe out all
traces of evidence as well as the base.

119
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:45,646
This stratum would be doomed.

120
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:49,642
For the time being, we'll
do more reconnaissance.

121
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:51,450
Emergency!

122
00:06:51,533 --> 00:06:53,677
The Dog Mountain Stratum
Lord is on its way!

123
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:57,701
Instruct all the inhabitants to
transfer to Clearflow Lake Stratum!

124
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:18,460
It's a mighty big wave,
big enough to do us all in.

125
00:07:30,740 --> 00:07:32,900
Listen up, we're evacuating.

126
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:35,337
The women and children take priority.

127
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:37,837
The tiny director can handle
getting everyone out of here.

128
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:41,260
As for us, we gotta stop
that dangerous Decay!

129
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:44,117
The way it's emerging
from the water is like

130
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:48,460
We could call it Dogzilla!

131
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:51,837
I'm not feeling confident we
can beat a whole mountain.

132
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:55,557
What did you guys do to fight back
the last time this thing attacked?

133
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:57,260
You remember Grams?

134
00:07:57,380 --> 00:08:01,145
Sometimes it really seems like
Grams here is going senile on me.

135
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:05,277
We wound up in the thing's belly, then
went completely ballistic on its insides.

136
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:06,190
Hmm.

137
00:08:06,273 --> 00:08:07,103
It was a close fight.

138
00:08:07,186 --> 00:08:08,016
We barely won.

139
00:08:08,380 --> 00:08:10,321
Whoa, so you've beaten it before?

140
00:08:10,420 --> 00:08:12,937
Sure, but I was essentially
a cub when we did it,

141
00:08:13,020 --> 00:08:16,597
and we only narrowly secured victory
by hacking away at its innards.

142
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:19,557
Even though I was there,
it still seems nuts to me.

143
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:21,287
We were almost doggy kibble.

144
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:24,157
You did it once, so
we'll just do it again.

145
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:25,117
That's reckless.

146
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:26,677
It's treacherous in there.

147
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:29,937
Its stomach is filled with burning
gastric acid for digestion,

148
00:08:30,020 --> 00:08:32,357
so the average person would
dissolve in an instant.

149
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:36,852
Back in the day, we only dared to
challenge it after months of preparation.

150
00:08:36,940 --> 00:08:38,060
He's got a point.

151
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:40,857
I vote for not burning
to death in a pup's tum.

152
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:43,646
In that case, our only
option is to get out...

153
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:45,000
We'll do it.

154
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:46,280
Pity and Voxo.

155
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:49,680
We'll attack from up
in the sky. Okay, then.

156
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:54,477
If it's useful, feel free to use the
magic items I made that can freeze water.

157
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,390
Are you ready?

158
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:56,780
Let's do this.

159
00:08:57,020 --> 00:08:58,820
Time to fly. Hello there!

160
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:00,580
Listen, you.

161
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:02,480
Be sure to come back to me.

162
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:04,830
Yes.

163
00:09:04,913 --> 00:09:06,800
You know it. Thank you.

164
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:11,400
I'll hold off on fixing that.

165
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:15,413
Judge me not, but the damage
makes me feel closer to her.

166
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:21,000
Alright, go time!

167
00:09:25,580 --> 00:09:26,860
It didn't work.

168
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:28,239
Not even a little.

169
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:30,408
We'll go the Hulemy route.

170
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:34,200
Do your thing, magic items!

171
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:49,900
Wow, it's frozen.

172
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:53,929
That bought us a teensy bit of
time, but it won't last long.

173
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:56,720
Here we go!

174
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:01,900
Oh, she may like some
of the nice juicy wave.

175
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:03,629
I'll take me some of that.

176
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:13,920
We showed the big dog who the big dog is.

177
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:19,380
But now we got a scurry for our lives.

178
00:10:21,940 --> 00:10:24,705
Won't be long before it
starts rampaging again.

179
00:10:24,980 --> 00:10:29,039
At least we got everyone out before
this place is swallowed by waves.

180
00:10:29,220 --> 00:10:30,050
Darn it.

181
00:10:30,133 --> 00:10:32,140
So much for having my own stratum.

182
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:34,732
I'll miss my unelected position of power.

183
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:39,880
The directors figured out
housing for all the evacuees.

184
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,940
And I wanted to do my part, too.

185
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:45,964
So I decided to welcome the
newcomers with a generous flash sale.

186
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:50,560
To ease the sting of losing their
homes, they get a 90 % discount.

187
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:55,377
I'm doling out freebies to folks who
only brought the clothes on their backs.

188
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:59,578
Any vending machine worth its salt
would choose kindness over profits.

189
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:08,260
The Clear Flow Lake Stratum's kinda peak.

190
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:10,897
We already have food and
shelter pretty much on lock,

191
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:13,862
though there was a
short-lived fashion emergency.

192
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:16,904
But then we held the
Dungeon Goddess Grand Prix,

193
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,294
awakening everyone's inner fashionista.

194
00:11:19,460 --> 00:11:22,754
This heralded the start of a
stratum-wide fashion craze.

195
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:25,420
Now everyone's Gouda on food,

196
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:28,877
clothing and shelter But what's
life without some jollies?

197
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:29,900
Speaking of,

198
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:32,097
the local men of culture
Were not so patiently

199
00:11:32,180 --> 00:11:34,533
awaiting the reopening of a certain shop

200
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:41,460
Shirley recruited yours truly
to draw in new customers

201
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:44,440
Hey there, cutie

202
00:11:45,280 --> 00:11:48,380
If you're feeling thirsty,
why not come inside?

203
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:51,400
Forget the sody, Bob!

204
00:11:51,540 --> 00:11:52,440
I want to live!

205
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:55,520
Welcome, our new friend,
ladies. Thank you.

206
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:57,740
Keep up the great work, Boxo.

207
00:11:58,620 --> 00:11:59,450
Oof.

208
00:11:59,533 --> 00:12:02,317
Not even a vending machine can
resist those feminine wiles.

209
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:04,165
But I'm a one-woman appliance.

210
00:12:08,040 --> 00:12:09,460
You're a real lifesaver.

211
00:12:09,760 --> 00:12:13,701
I'm sure Rosie and me, the dog
fiend, is going to love these gifts.

212
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:16,437
You'd be surprised how
many people attempt to

213
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:18,537
buy the affections of
these ladies of the night.

214
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:22,700
My sage-advice and unique range
of products are hot commodities,

215
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:25,440
so I'm essentially the village wingman.

216
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:29,100
Poxo. G-Oarch?

217
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:31,360
Help me out. Hello there.

218
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:32,960
What do you know?

219
00:12:33,140 --> 00:12:35,437
Even Gorth is in the mood for some lovin'.

220
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:40,461
Well, um, yeah, I was wondering if you had
thoughts on what Miss Shirley would like.

221
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:42,320
You wanna woo Miss Shirley?

222
00:12:42,980 --> 00:12:44,840
Slow your roll, Icarus!

223
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,717
You're flying way too close to the sun!

224
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:49,300
We're talking lunatic mode with no saves,

225
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:52,715
a hopeless quest in a romantic
hell of your own making.

226
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:55,400
I really want to please her.

227
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:58,637
I know she likes cash payments.

228
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:02,308
Outside of that, I actually
don't know a whole lot about her.

229
00:13:03,060 --> 00:13:04,777
I'm back. Understood.

230
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:06,420
I can check back in later.

231
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:10,220
I'm the same metal box who
helped Karyos find love.

232
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:14,793
The completionist in me would love to
couple up his partner Gorth as well.

233
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:16,180
I'm on the case.

234
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:21,682
In the name of love, I'll find out what
kind of non-dirty stuff Miss Shirley likes.

235
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:25,960
I knew I was going to need
backup, so I enlisted Lamas,

236
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:28,600
Hulemy, and Suco to help dig up the deets.

237
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:34,220
Is this really close enough to
Miss Shirley's house? Hello there.

238
00:13:34,620 --> 00:13:35,940
Clue one acquired.

239
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:38,897
She works in an extravagant den of sin,

240
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:41,737
but lives in a house
that's pretty run-of-mill.

241
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:43,977
We're going to go and have a look inside.

242
00:13:44,060 --> 00:13:46,001
Holler if you see someone coming.

243
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:48,000
I'd better go incognito.

244
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:50,946
It would be bad if Miss
Shirley recognized me.

245
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:56,970
Hmm?

246
00:13:57,520 --> 00:13:58,350
Huh?

247
00:13:59,960 --> 00:14:02,900
It's like they got their
garb from Sus R Us.

248
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:04,100
But it's fine.

249
00:14:04,340 --> 00:14:06,817
Maybe they're just going
for a nice little stroll.

250
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:09,429
Well, so much for the
benefit of the doubt.

251
00:14:10,260 --> 00:14:12,440
Oops. Oh, cool. You talking to me?

252
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:14,040
Well, you're the end.

253
00:14:16,140 --> 00:14:17,620
I'll go scare him off!

254
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,040
Total overkill!

255
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:27,057
You can't disturb the peace
this early in the a .m.

256
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:27,970
Told ya!

257
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:29,020
How very odd.

258
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:32,399
I could have sworn I heard
a rabid animal screaming.

259
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,468
Suppose it was a bad dream.

260
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:39,040
Oh, wow.

261
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:41,264
She's just as alluring at home.

262
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:44,840
Hey, she's leaving.

263
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:51,124
Miss Shirley looks good in a dress, but
she's a real smoke show in that red vinyl.

264
00:14:51,380 --> 00:14:53,792
It's like a naughty version of my outfit.

265
00:14:53,900 --> 00:14:56,665
Helps that you don't have
bare skin or honkers.

266
00:14:57,120 --> 00:14:58,061
I'll follow her.

267
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:09,197
She's supposed to have the whole day off.

268
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:10,237
Wonder where she's going.

269
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:13,202
I honestly can't imagine
how she spends her time.

270
00:15:13,460 --> 00:15:14,580
I can't either.

271
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:19,217
My first thought was a fancy lunch at
some pricey restaurant or something.

272
00:15:19,300 --> 00:15:21,359
She's not exactly dressed for that.

273
00:15:21,740 --> 00:15:22,975
Where's Miss Shirley?

274
00:15:27,520 --> 00:15:28,350
Hang on.

275
00:15:28,620 --> 00:15:30,437
Isn't that place the local orphanage?

276
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:31,460
It sure is.

277
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:34,597
I know because Shui and I
paid them a visit recently.

278
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:37,739
Us glutton swing by sometimes
to play with the kids.

279
00:15:39,280 --> 00:15:43,574
Think she came to cheer them up about
the whole not having parents thing?

280
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:45,040
Hello, hello!

281
00:15:45,660 --> 00:15:47,240
Hooray! It's Miss Shirley!

282
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:49,117
Which game do you want to play?

283
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:50,553
That's a game you fall!

284
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:52,137
Will you throw it or something?

285
00:15:52,220 --> 00:15:53,420
We'll play in a bit.

286
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:56,117
I need to have a word
with the director first.

287
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:58,297
After that, I'll throw
the ball or something.

288
00:15:58,380 --> 00:15:59,210
Well, hot dog!

289
00:15:59,380 --> 00:16:00,210
Hey, director!

290
00:16:00,293 --> 00:16:02,117
Miss Shirley says she
needs to talk to you!

291
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,030
I know.

292
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:04,885
I could hear her very clearly.

293
00:16:05,380 --> 00:16:08,360
Miss Shirley, it's always
a pleasure to see you.

294
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:10,992
It's nice to see the children so excited.

295
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:12,896
Anyway, here you go.

296
00:16:13,080 --> 00:16:14,374
It's the usual amount.

297
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:18,137
I could never thank you enough
for all your generous donations.

298
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:19,985
Please, make yourself at home.

299
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:21,600
You're too kind.

300
00:16:22,140 --> 00:16:25,340
Turns out, she's
literally helping orphans.

301
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:27,457
My brain's remembering something.

302
00:16:27,540 --> 00:16:30,257
Shui said Miss Shirley's
also in the No Parents Club.

303
00:16:30,340 --> 00:16:32,917
It turns out Miss Shirley's
kind of an incredible person.

304
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,059
She's a prime example of womankind.

305
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:38,397
If I were a human male, I'd
kill to take her out to dinner.

306
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:40,437
Yeah, I'd even spring for dessert.

307
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:41,755
Can't say I disagree.

308
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:43,050
Poor Gorth.

309
00:16:43,133 --> 00:16:46,417
If she's the major leagues, he's
still playing t-ball in the backyard.

310
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:48,917
She's like an ancient
goddess princess angel you

311
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,824
can't have unless you
slay a dragon blindfolded.

312
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:56,057
I'm starting to feel like maybe it
was wrong of us to stalk her all day.

313
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:57,077
Yeah, maybe so.

314
00:16:57,160 --> 00:17:00,637
Let's apologize and play with the kids
to prove we're not terrible people.

315
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:01,550
I'll play Mr.

316
00:17:01,633 --> 00:17:03,266
Bear even though I'm not one.

317
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,780
Hey, everyone! Wow!

318
00:17:05,020 --> 00:17:06,617
We're gonna run out of chairs!

319
00:17:06,700 --> 00:17:07,530
Hurry!

320
00:17:07,613 --> 00:17:08,443
Come play with us!

321
00:17:09,420 --> 00:17:10,880
Well, look who it is.

322
00:17:11,080 --> 00:17:12,737
Did you get tired of tailing me?

323
00:17:12,820 --> 00:17:13,879
You saw that, huh?

324
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:16,200
I'm sorry for stalking you.

325
00:17:16,380 --> 00:17:19,257
We got carried away wanting
to know more about you.

326
00:17:19,340 --> 00:17:20,500
I feel awful.

327
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:22,837
We let Curiosity get the best of us.

328
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:24,960
Please don't be mad. Sorry.

329
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:26,361
You're forgiven.

330
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:31,317
But if you'd like to make amends, stick
around and spend some time with the kids.

331
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:32,230
Deal!

332
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:33,720
Mr. Bear time!

333
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:36,788
Which one of you wants
to be the bear first?

334
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:50,340
It warms the circuitry I call a
heart to see the joy on their faces.

335
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,497
Thank you for visiting.

336
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:56,815
You're welcome to come see us anytime.

337
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:59,298
I look forward to serving you again.

338
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:06,581
Not to keep prying, but is this
always how you spend your off days?

339
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:09,177
Guess I never really thought about it.

340
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:11,277
I don't enjoy shopping very much,

341
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:14,677
and I'm constantly bringing
delicious leftovers home from work.

342
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:17,720
Very rarely indulge in dining out. Really?

343
00:18:18,140 --> 00:18:21,220
She spends her nights in a
dazzling world of excess,

344
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:23,892
but is not wasteful or indulgent herself.

345
00:18:24,220 --> 00:18:27,780
She's pretty, friendly, nice
to kids, and open-minded.

346
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:30,768
Miss Shirley's in the
running for best girl!

347
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:38,060
Hello there.

348
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:40,960
Tell me, did you figure anything out?

349
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:44,700
You want me to watch something?

350
00:18:52,140 --> 00:18:54,400
I won't let them get away with that.

351
00:18:54,860 --> 00:18:56,272
Figured that would work.

352
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:59,400
I'll let him handle the
creepy trench coat brigade.

353
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:15,997
Seems she's even more
wonderful than I imagined.

354
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:16,910
Yes!

355
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:21,200
She'd never fall for a guy like me.

356
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:23,940
It's like a shoe loving a sock. Huh?

357
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:25,620
Quickest forfeit ever.

358
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:29,597
Guess I'll just have to be content with
watching her thrive from a distance.

359
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:31,562
I don't want to stir up trouble.

360
00:19:36,120 --> 00:19:38,757
That's a surprisingly
depressing turn of events.

361
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:40,797
But that's the choice he's making.

362
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:43,240
And the customer is always right.

363
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:46,757
I've been helping Miss Shirley.

364
00:19:46,840 --> 00:19:48,517
Get things rolling at her shop.

365
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:49,997
For about a week now.

366
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:52,040
But today's the last day.

367
00:19:53,040 --> 00:19:54,820
Come back and see us soon.

368
00:19:55,680 --> 00:19:57,137
Have a wonderful night.

369
00:19:57,220 --> 00:19:58,100
I will now.

370
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:03,510
Weird.

371
00:20:03,700 --> 00:20:04,641
Something's off.

372
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:06,270
Charlie!

373
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:08,400
Oh, I'm sorry.

374
00:20:09,220 --> 00:20:12,573
It's just that there's something
I can't get off my mind.

375
00:20:12,740 --> 00:20:15,328
If you have time, I'd
love to talk about it.

376
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:16,660
Yes, yes.

377
00:20:18,380 --> 00:20:22,597
A neighbor told me there's been a lot
of suspicious activity around my house,

378
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:25,997
particularly some interesting
characters being kind of pervy.

379
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:27,760
Yup, them's the facts.

380
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:31,617
I've even had my underwear stolen
while it was hanging out to dry.

381
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:34,357
But that sort of thing
hasn't been happening lately.

382
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:36,320
And those pervy men are gone.

383
00:20:36,600 --> 00:20:38,340
It's great, but strange.

384
00:20:38,760 --> 00:20:40,040
So that's it.

385
00:20:40,180 --> 00:20:42,337
She's in the dark about
Gorth's white knighting.

386
00:20:42,420 --> 00:20:44,560
Oh, speaking of...

387
00:20:46,580 --> 00:20:50,780
Hey, Boxo, did I make it in
time? Too bad! That's a shame.

388
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:53,857
I was hoping to have a
drink before heading home.

389
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:56,540
I'd love a nightcap if
you don't mind. Same.

390
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:59,233
That's the best idea I've heard in ages.

391
00:20:59,860 --> 00:21:04,140
After all, I've hardly had a
drop to drink today. It's you!

392
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:05,510
I...

393
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:08,840
You're easily one of my
best customers. Really.

394
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:10,820
Chill out, my guy.

395
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:12,240
You got this.

396
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:15,856
You're the greatest.

397
00:21:16,340 --> 00:21:17,460
Thanks a lot, Boxo.

398
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:21,240
Here's to a hard day's work. Right.

399
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:22,382
Cheers to that.

400
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:28,670
Poor thing.

401
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:31,297
It must be difficult to
work such late hours.

402
00:21:31,380 --> 00:21:32,380
Oh, it's fine.

403
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:34,326
I mean, you know how it goes.

404
00:21:35,760 --> 00:21:38,657
If I could vend love, I'd do it.

405
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:40,797
But the best I can do is late-night booze.

406
00:21:40,880 --> 00:21:43,056
Still, I'll be rooting for these two.

407
00:21:43,540 --> 00:21:47,069
It's a crying shame you can't
enjoy a cold beverage with us.

408
00:21:47,420 --> 00:21:51,008
Honestly, I'd be thrilled to
share a midnight drink with you.

409
00:21:51,260 --> 00:21:52,090
Ixnay!

410
00:21:52,173 --> 00:21:56,080
I know I'm tall, dark, and well-stocked,
But now is so not the time.

411
00:21:56,960 --> 00:21:57,790
Poxo.

412
00:21:59,580 --> 00:22:00,410
Zoinks!

413
00:22:00,493 --> 00:22:01,437
If looks could kill?

414
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:04,402
I'd be in the great factory
in the sky about now.

415
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:51,957
Bota

416
00:22:53,866 --> 00:22:54,696
Mustady.

417
00:23:01,170 --> 00:23:02,000
It's a story for you.

418
00:23:02,083 --> 00:23:06,257
I'm waiting for you, I'm waiting for you!

419
00:23:06,340 --> 00:23:09,540
I'm waiting for you, I'm feeling you!

420
00:23:11,500 --> 00:23:13,897
I'm not funny, I know you are!

421
00:23:13,980 --> 00:23:15,020
I know you are!

422
00:23:17,260 --> 00:23:20,740
I'm not good at all, I'm not good at all.

423
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:37,980
I look forward to serving you again.
